course: dictionary
lesson: 1891
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Context tells you which meaning the writer wants. Read the whole sentence, then ask: which meaning fits here? Look for clue words around it.
explain: Cologne is a good example. «She dabbed a little cologne behind her ears before the party.» Here cologne is a light, sweet-smelling perfume, often for men. Dabbed and ears tell you it is something you put on your skin, not a place.
explain: Now read this: «Rhine cities like Cologne grow rich from tolls.» The word Cologne has a capital letter and is a city. A capital letter in the middle of a sentence is a clue: it often marks the name of a place or a person.
fact: Cologne means a light perfume, often for men, and it is also called eau de cologne.
fact: Cologne, with a capital C, is a large city on the River Rhine in western Germany.
fact: In German the city is called Köln.
fact: Cologne Cathedral is famous for its huge Gothic church building. It took about 600 years to build and survived bombing in the Second World War.
fact: The perfume was named after the city where it was first made in the 1700s.
exercise: «He splashed on some cologne before going out.» What is cologne here? | A tall church tower | A kind of soup | * A light perfume | A city in Germany
exercise: «Cologne Cathedral took about 600 years to build.» What does Cologne mean in this sentence? | A river in Spain | * A large city in western Germany | A light perfume | A type of bottle
exercise: In the middle of a sentence, what does a capital letter often show? | * It shows a name, such as a place or a person | It shows the word is very important | It shows the word is an animal | It shows the sentence is a question
test: «Rhine cities like Cologne grow rich from tolls.» Which meaning fits best? | A light perfume | * A city on a river | A type of tall tree
test: In «She dabbed cologne behind her ears», which word tells you it is a smell? | * Dabbed | Before | She | Ears
exam: A friend says cologne is only a city. Which fact shows that is wrong? | Cologne is a type of bread | Cologne is a river in Germany | Cologne is a city, so it cannot also be a smell | * Cologne is also a light perfume, often for men
